					<h1>Grand Prize Award Winner</h1>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Name:</strong> Madison Bella</li>
						<li><strong>Age:</strong> 9</li>
						<li><strong>Award:</strong> $5,000 to the Soaring Eagles youth group, plus Mia's Starter Collection</li>
						<li><strong>Nominated by:</strong> Her mother, Jennifer</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div id="essay">
					<h2>Sharing her culture through dance</h2>
					<p>Madison Bella&#8217;s family roots are woven into the tapestry of our nation&#8217;s history&#8212;she is part Native American and part Caucasian.  It can be difficult growing up biracial.  Madison Bella knows she must walk between cultures.</p>
					<p class="pullquote">Madison Bella&#8217;s group teaches kids about native cultures, including their music, dance, and history.</p>
					<p>When Madison Bella was younger, her family moved from a reservation to the Midwest. While she missed the mountains and the people, she found amazing strength in herself.  Instead of being sad about starting over, Madison Bella listened to her heart and discovered the beat of the drum calling her.  It was the beat of a powwow.</p>
					<p>Madison Bella started watching and learning from champion native dancers.  She practiced at home to perfect her moves. Last year, she began placing in contest powwows&#8212;third, second, then first.</p>
					<p>But she didn&#8217;t stop there.  She&#8217;s been taught that her people must complete the circle and give back. Madison Bella went to her elders with the idea of a youth group, and Soaring Eagles was soon born.  The group teaches kids about native cultures, including their music, dance, and history. The group now encompasses many tribes and families throughout her state.</p>
					<p>Madison Bella continues to dance and teach others as well. She&#8217;s also learning more of her traditions and ways, then helping younger kids learn those same ways.  She&#8217;s become a championship dancer herself and a role model for her native community, getting good grades and contributing as a family member.</p>
					<p class="last">Madison Bella has found her niche bridging two worlds and learned that she can be a role model, showing pride in who she is and where she&#8217;s from.</p>
				</div>
